  "description": "Shenora's Windows shell: application bootstrapper with global exception handling, DPI-correct window-state persistence, one instance per install, a later launch handing the running app its arguments, secondary windows on their own STA threads, tray icon, frameless-chrome form, and the Windows implementations of the Shenora shell contracts (STA file dialogs, clipboard, shell launching, UI-thread dispatcher). Hosts WebView2: environment prewarm, dev-server vs packaged-frontend loading, navigation/new-window/download/permission/process-failure handling, drag-drop zones, and the postMessage IPC bridge with batched event push. Hosts Chromium the same way, through Shenora.Chromium: a ChromiumView control, with UseChromiumEngine running CEF beside the WinForms loop; reference Shenora.Chromium from the app itself, since CEF arrives only through that package's build. Hosts the auxiliary browser sessions (Shenora.Core.Sessions) in WebView2: WebView2SessionHost makes their off-screen browsers and an interactive session's modal window.",
